## 21. Pakistan-wide dynamic geocoding verification
- [ ] Existing geocoding audit
  - Acceptance: reviewed current geocoding implementation; no hardcoded city database; dynamic search via Open-Meteo API
- [ ] API parameter verification
  - Acceptance: verified `country_code=PK` parameter works with Open-Meteo geocoding API; confirmed it prioritises Pakistani results for unqualified city names without excluding valid worldwide results
- [ ] Pakistan-first query strategy
  - Acceptance: unqualified city names (no comma) such as "Haripur" automatically resolve to Pakistani locations; queries with explicit country context (comma-separated) such as "Paris, France" are handled by the ranking algorithm's explicit-context logic
- [ ] Country-qualified search
  - Acceptance: "Lahore, Pakistan" → Lahore, Pakistan; "Paris, France" → Paris, France; "Paris, Texas" → Paris, Texas, USA; "Lahore, Virginia" → US Lahore; "qzxnotarealcity" → city not found error
- [ ] Global fallback
  - Acceptance: if Pakistan filter returns no suitable result for a given city name, the normal (unfiltered) geocoding request is used and the ranking algorithm selects the best global match
- [ ] Haripur exact-match test
  - Acceptance: user enters "Haripur" → application resolves "Haripur, Khyber Pakhtunkhwa, Pakistan" → uses exact geocoded coordinates (lat 33.99783, lon 72.93493) → retrieves and displays genuine weather for that location
- [ ] Province-wise location coverage
  - Acceptance: tested representative cities across all Pakistani provinces and regions:
    - Khyber Pakhtunkhwa: Haripur, Abbottabad, Mansehra, Peshawar, Mardan, Mingora, Nowshera, Kohat, Bannu, Dera Ismail Khan, Chitral
    - Punjab: Lahore, Faisalabad, Rawalpindi, Multan, Gujranwala, Sialkot, Bahawalpur, Sargodha, Sheikhupura, Kasur, Okara, Sahiwal, Rahim Yar Khan, Dera Ghazi Khan
    - Sindh: Karachi, Hyderabad, Sukkur, Larkana, Khairpur, Jacobabad, Shaheed Benazirabad
    - Balochistan: Quetta, Gwadar, Turbat, Khuzdar
    - Islamabad Capital Territory: Islamabad
    - Azad Jammu and Kashmir: Muzaffarabad, Mirpur
    - Gilgit-Baltistan: Gilgit, Skardu
  - For each test city: records actual geocoding result (name, country, admin1, feature code, coordinates, timezone) and weather result availability
- [ ] Alternate-name tests
  - Acceptance: supported alternate names and spellings resolve correctly via live geocoding (e.g. Nawabshah / Shaheed Benazirabad, Mingora as Swat-region reference)
  - Aliases must only improve the query sent to geocoding; the displayed location and coordinates must always come from an actual verified geocoding result
- [ ] Location-coordinate validation
  - Acceptance: before requesting weather, verifies result has actual location name, finite latitude/longitude within valid ranges (‑90 to 90, ‑180 to 180), country information handled safely, and selected place is appropriate for the query
- [ ] Weather integration validation
  - Acceptance: for successful locations, verifies HTTP success, valid JSON, correct coordinates used in weather API request, current weather availability, valid temperature, correct units (°C/°F), valid timezone, forecast data availability
- [ ] Timezone validation
  - Acceptance: for all successfully resolved Pakistani locations, uses the location's returned timezone (e.g. Asia/Karachi); preserves local forecast timestamps; displays local time correctly; does not rely on user's browser timezone; handles missing timezone gracefully
- [ ] Existing regression tests
  - Acceptance: re-run the application's existing test suites (ranking tests, conversion tests, e2e tests); all previously passing behaviors preserved; `node --check js/app.js` passes
- [ ] Browser verification
  - Acceptance: verified in actual browser:
    1. Enter "Haripur" → confirmed result is Haripur, Khyber Pakhtunkhwa, Pakistan
    2. No unnecessary location-selection popup appears
    3. Actual coordinates are used in the weather request
    4. Weather result appears
    5. Other Pakistani cities search successfully
    6. International city search remains functional (Tokyo, London, Paris)
